            <ArticleTitle>Novel Reassortant Highly Pathogenic Avian Influenza (H5N8) Virus in Zoos, India.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>717-719</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid2304.161886</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Highly pathogenic avian influenza (H5N8) viruses were detected in waterfowl at 2 zoos in India in October 2016. Both viruses were different 7:1 reassortants of H5N8 viruses isolated in May 2016 from wild birds in the Russian Federation and China, suggesting virus spread during southward winter migration of birds.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
